# --- Orchestrator monitoring ---------------------------------------------
# The shared monitoring module is stateless, and as of 2026-07-28 it is
# ENFORCED rather than tolerated: status.sh exits 2 instead of spooling into
# the module dir, and both daemons exit 1 rather than falling back to it. The
# two ignore lines that used to sanction that leak
# (.claude/shared/monitoring/{events.jsonl,.watcher-state.json}) are gone on
# purpose — tests/test_bootstrap.py asserts they stay gone, so the behaviour
# cannot quietly return under cover of an ignore rule.

# LEGACY DEFENCE (kept deliberately, G9/LAYOUT-4). Per-task orchestration run
# state is local working data, kept on disk for monitor replay and the Mongo
# legacy keyspace but no longer versioned (untracked 2026-07-27). Since the
# tasks-root move the live tree is `.touch/local-orchestrators/`, ignored by the
# `/.touch/*` rule below; these three lines stay so a RE-CREATED old tree is
# still ignored rather than silently offered for commit. They also remain in the
# verbatim guard lists in tests/test_bootstrap.py and monitoring's test_shell.py.
.claude/local-orchestrators/
.claude/local-orchestrators/*/*.log
.claude/local-orchestrators/*/.watcher-state.json

# --- Touch runtime state --------------------------------------------------
# `.touch/` holds five trust classes in one directory, so the rule is an
# ALLOWLIST: everything under it is ignored, and exactly the files that are
# meant to be public are re-included by name. The ORDER of the five memory
# lines is the mechanism, not a style choice — git cannot re-include a file
# under an excluded DIRECTORY, so `memory/` is re-included as a directory
# BEFORE its children are re-ignored except `*.md` (G9). The twin of this list
# is tests/test_bootstrap.py's GITIGNORE_ENTRIES; keep them character-for-
# character identical.
# PROVENANCE: the three memory lines were RESTORED here, not authored here —
# G9 decided them and tests/test_bootstrap.py has demanded them since d666ce8,
# but the commit that rewrote `.touch/` into `/.touch/*` dropped them, leaving
# three suites red against the repo's own law. D-12 opened this file for the
# `run.json` carve below, and the repair landed in the same, correctly ordered
# block. Anyone auditing why several suites went green inside one
# templates-only change-set: this is why.
/.touch/*
/.touch?*/
!/.touch/memory/
/.touch/memory/*
!/.touch/memory/*.md
# The second carve, and the only other one (D-12/SKILLS-7): the tracked
# per-project run constants — targeted/full test commands, the known baseline,
# the review checklist — that `touch-run start` merges UNDER a run spec before
# handing `args` to a workflow template. It is configuration, not state, and it
# is a single FILE, so no directory re-include is needed. Never widen this
# carve: a token file or a watcher checkpoint must never become committable.
!/.touch/run.json
*.pid

# Per-machine harness overrides (never shared, may hold local paths/secrets).
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Mongo mirror ---------------------------------------------------------
# No Mongo data directory and no dump ever lives inside the repo: the mirror
# holds the same unredacted transcripts .touch/ exists to protect.
mongo-data/
mongo-dump/
# *.bson is unanchored on purpose (dumps land wherever mongodump is run). If a
# .bson ever needs to be a committed test fixture, negate it explicitly rather
# than narrowing this rule: !tests/fixtures/**/*.bson
*.bson

